{
  "_comment": [
    "The DEFAULT dashboard's stored config, in its pre-migration location.",
    "",
    "This file is the seed for a shape hactl believed impossible. Home Assistant 2026.x",
    "migrates a stored default into the dashboards collection at boot",
    "(_async_migrate_default_config, storage mode only): it creates an entry with url_path",
    "`lovelace` and mode `storage`, moves this file to .storage/lovelace.lovelace, and deletes",
    "this one. So after the first boot lovelace/dashboards/list reports the default — under a",
    "url_path a user-created dashboard cannot take, with mode `storage`.",
    "",
    "hactl read `the default is listed` as `the default is YAML-mode`, because the only",
    "instance state that had ever produced a listed default was the YAML one",
    "(internal/integration/lovelace_oracle_test.go, captured before this migration existed).",
    "`dash save` and `dash replace` therefore refused the default on the reference instance,",
    "citing a `lovelace: mode: yaml` line its configuration.yaml does not contain.",
    "",
    "HA performs the migration itself from this file, which is the whole reason the fixture",
    "seeds the OLD location: if a future HA stops migrating, the rig stops carrying the shape",
    "and TestRigFixtureDefaultDashboardIsListedAsStorage says so instead of quietly passing."
